 "pinned_files_note": "These decide which values a decision may read: the bindings set each series' availability time and first publication, the definitions and schedule set the inputs, and the calendars set the sessions. A ticket is refused if any differs. The hashes here are the draft's and are set again when it is registered; changing one afterwards is an amendment.",
 "state_rule": "On a session with a score, the state is the gate's procedure applied to that session's snapshot: every session with a score in that data counts toward the thresholds and toward the three-session step-down, whether or not a ticket was issued for it. On a session without a score, because an input was missing, the ticket carries the state of the issuer's last live ticket of the same gate and subject and the step-down count starts again; with no such ticket, a gap is recorded and no state. A session with no ticket at all is a missed ticket: for exposure it holds the last live ticket's state, as RFC-006 section 3.3 says.",
